Do not require Qualcomm SDE plane capabilities to initialize the display.

The rebased minui ("twrpminui: rebase graphics and input on current minui")
selects primary planes by looking for a "capabilities" plane property and
parsing the primary_smart_plane_id marker out of its blob.  That property is a
Qualcomm SDE extension; mediatek-drm creates only the standard DRM plane
properties.

Initdisplay() therefore finds no candidate plane on this MTK device:

  TWRP DRM: display 0 found 0/2 primary planes for CRTC index 0
  Failed to init display
  gui2: minui display initialization failed

MinuiBackendDrm::Init() returns nullptr, GUI2 exits, init restarts recovery,
and the kernel keeps showing the bootloader logo while adbd stays reachable
over its own USB function - the device looks hung at the OnePlus logo although
"adb devices" lists it.

Probe the plane property once.  When it is missing, keep the pre-rebase
behaviour: walk the plane list forward and use the first planes that can drive
the connector's CRTC.  Qualcomm devices keep the reverse CLO order.

